 comment, I am excited. And whoever writes I am excited in the comment, I will give heart to all those comments. In this video, we will learn to link an HTML website with CSS and JavaScript. Along with that, in this video, I am going to give you guys notes, cheat sheets and many more resources. I will tell you guys some techniques that I have learned in years. And it will literally make your web development speed 10x. In this video, we will also see how to make our VS Code awesome. So that your VS Code screen will look killer. In this video, I will also tell you guys how to earn money from web development. So let's start with full energy. Let's roll the intro. Alright guys, so we have come to our computer screen. Before moving forward in the video, I would like to tell you all that do access this playlist. Secondly, we are very close to 5 million subscribers. So if you guys have not hit the subscribe, then do it. In today's video, we are going to make our first website, as I told you. The first thing we will do is to customize our VS Code. So this is the folder in which we started our web development series. Now I have to give you the source code of this web development series. So I will configure the git here. Now it is not at all necessary for you to know about git. But I will fire the GitHub desktop here. And what I will do here is that I will add a new repository. I will click on add here. I will click on create new repository. I will name it as Sigma web dev course. And this is our folder. So I will select this folder. I will initialize this repository with readme. And I will write source code for Sigma web development course here. I will click on create repository. By doing this, a repository will be created here, whose name is Sigma web dev course. I will put all the things that were relevant from the first video here. So these two files were relevant from the first video. So I will name it as video 1. Right click, new folder. I will make a video 1 here. And I will move these two files to video 1 folder. I am not pushing all these videos on git. These are sample videos. You can use your sample videos. So now whatever the source code will be, I will update it here. And I will keep pushing it on git here. Now how do we push it on git here? You don't need to learn this. But this procedure is very simple. Why do we use git? I would like to tell you that git is used by web developers. And then general coders use it. When they have to collaborate their code with other people. So what will happen is that you will work with many programmers. And those programmers will collaborate with your source code. And to do this kind of collaboration, they will also push some code. You will also push some code. Maybe one person is editing a file. One person is editing another file. So here github comes into use. And what is github desktop? Github desktop is a utility to use git. The difference between git and github is that git is open source. But github is a Microsoft-owned company. Which helps you to host repositories on your web interface using git. I will tell you more about git in the coming videos. But I am pushing this repository on my codewithhari github account. So you will get the repository link in the description. So as I give you links, if you follow them, you will get all the code. And I will talk about it later. I am making this video, the course, an impact. In such a way that absolute beginners can follow it. So as soon as I click on the published repository, this code, this folder will sync with my github account. So all the code that I am going to upload here, it will go to my github account and will keep syncing. The changes that will be here, will be there. If someone has made changes there, I can pull it here. I can pull it by clicking here, by doing fetch origin. I will teach you all this. We will dedicate a whole video to git. You don't worry at all. I did this thing so that I can give you code. Now I will make a fol